menu "KVMpad secure remote"

    config KVM_SRT_MAX_SOCKETS
        int "Concurrent TLS sockets on the remote port"
        range 2 5
        default 3
        help
            Upper bound on sockets the WebSocket server accepts at once. One socket is needed for
            the pairing endpoint while a window is open, the rest for control sessions; the session
            glue refuses anything past its own limit with HTTP 503 regardless of this value.

            Each TLS socket costs roughly 40 kB while the handshake runs, so this is the dominant
            RAM knob of the whole feature. Raise it only if several CLIENTs really have to be
            connected at the same time (FR-721 needs one).

    config KVM_SRT_SOCKET_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Socket send/receive timeout (s)"
        range 1 10
        default 2
        help
            How long a socket read or write may block the server task. It is also the bound on how
            long a call from the UI task can wait for the transport lock, because the lock is held
            across a frame write. Lower values make a stalled peer cheaper and a slow network more
            likely to drop frames.

    config KVM_SRT_ADVERTISE_MDNS
        bool "Advertise _kvmpad._tcp over mDNS"
        default y
        help
            FR-723 service discovery. Takes effect only when the managed `espressif/mdns` component
            is part of the build; otherwise the advertisement is skipped and the CLIENT has to be
            given an address. The TXT record carries the device name, the protocol version and
            whether a pairing window is open -- never a code, a token or a certificate hash.

endmenu
